{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, happy to help you get ready for tomorrow's meeting. First, check the Company Portal (also called Software Center) on your laptop. Open it from the Start menu and search for \"Zoom\". If it's there, click Install. It installs on its own without IT, and you can use it right away. If Zoom isn't listed, we need your manager's approval and a quick security review before we can install it. To start that, ask your manager to reply to this ticket approving Zoom, with a line about why you need it (client meetings). We'll pass it along as soon as the approval comes in. Approval and review might not finish by tomorrow. As a backup, you may be able to join from the link in the client's Zoom invite using your web browser, without installing anything. Please reply and tell us whether you found Zoom in the Company Portal. One more thing: please don't install Zoom from a download link someone emails you.",
  "internal_note": "P4 software request: Zoom client for BL-LT-0106. User is Leo Martins (user_id 6), Sales, Account Executive. Account is active with no problems. Following KB-027, I asked the user to check the Company Portal first. I can't see the Portal catalogue with my tools, so I haven't confirmed whether Zoom is in it. If it isn't there, KB-027 requires manager approval plus a security review, so I've asked the user to get their manager to approve on this ticket. Once approval arrives, escalate to Tier 2 with: app Zoom Workplace client (latest stable), business reason (external client meetings), approver = the user's manager. No admin rights or credentials shared.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-027"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
